From: Abhishek Kunati <itsmekunati@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:24:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] octet: 10s block target and per-block LWMA difficulty

nPowTargetSpacing = 10 on all networks. GetNextWorkRequired now uses LWMA-1
(window 90 blocks, 60 on regtest) instead of the 2016-block retarget; regtest
keeps fixed minimum difficulty unless started with -test=lwma.
PermittedDifficultyTransition (headers-sync anti-DoS heuristic) now always
returns true because a per-block algorithm has no fixed boundary to bound.
nPowTargetTimespan is kept only as the reporting/versionbits period.
Main and testnet activate all soft forks from genesis.
